Found some shortcuts - Fn+1,2,3.  Added to sheet in First Post.<br>Wondering what else would make a good shortcut ???<br> - Fn+4: Cycle Scan modes (Stop, Pause, Hold, (Loop?))<br> - Fn+5: ?<br><br><strong class="text-strong">Question:.</strong><br> Fn+S1 temporarily swaps VFO Rx for Tx in FM mode. Maybe it should be just Tx to Rx ?<br>Reasoning:<br>I think primary use is for repeaters. I.e check if you can hear the talker on the input channel so you can then go Simplex.<br>Not sure of use case for DMR, probably the same? but I think most Amateurs use DMR to use internet to make long distance connects, and Emergency network.<br>But if Fn+S1 just copied the Tx to the Rx (so Tx freq is on both) then that might be more  <em class="text-italics">"correct"</em> as Transmitting would still work on repeater (Yes its a tricky hand manipulation to do that so not really sure this is a good idea) . Of course both work in practice.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=971">Zl1XE</a> — Tue Aug 18, 2020 3:57 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
